{%- comment -%}
  The theme's own emblem, drawn rather than shipped as artwork.

  It replaced three PNGs — a dark cut, a light cut and a spare, about 50KB
  between them — which were the previous shop's real logo. A theme for sale
  cannot carry another business's mark, and renaming the files did not change
  what was inside them.

  Inline SVG on `currentColor`, so:
    - it takes the colour of whatever surface it sits on, which is what the two
      cuts existed to fake, and it follows a merchant's colour scheme for free;
    - it costs no request and about 400 bytes against 50KB;
    - it stays sharp at any size, where the PNGs were fixed at 139x154.

  Deliberately generic: a lozenge with a girdle and two crown facets. It is a
  placeholder a merchant replaces in `wordmark_mark`, and it is drawn in the
  theme's own language — hairline, square-on, geometric — so a store that never
  replaces it still looks deliberate rather than unfinished.

  `stroke-width` is in the viewBox's own units and scales with the mark. Do not
  reach for `vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke` — see the loader's note; it is
  not needed here, and it destroys any future dash animation.

  Accepts:
    class - extra classes for the caller
{%- endcomment -%}

<svg
  class="lockup__mark{% if class != blank %} {{ class }}{% endif %}"
  viewBox="0 0 139 154"
  width="139"
  height="154"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="7"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
>
  <path d="M69.5 8 L131 77 L69.5 146 L8 77 Z" />
  <path d="M8 77 H131" />
  <path d="M40 42 L52 77 M99 42 L87 77" stroke-linecap="round" />
</svg>
